alue": "Association of national organizations of professional film critics Headquartered in Munich. Founded 1930.", "newValue": "The International Federation of Film Critics (FIPRESCI), established in 1930, is a global organization that unites national film critic associations, thereby playing a crucial role in the international film landscape. Headquartered in Munich, Germany, FIPRESCI emerged during a transformative period in cinema, when the medium was evolving rapidly, and film criticism was becoming essential to the art form's appreciation and understanding. Key figures in its founding included prominent critics from various countries, who recognized the necessity of a unified voice in film evaluation amidst the burgeoning global film industry.

